{"@context":["https://litlfred.github.io/folio-assistant/ns/content/v1.jsonld",{"@base":"https://litlfred.github.io/folio/"}],"@id":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/rem-brings-realisations","@type":["folio-assistant-core:Remark","doco:Section"],"label":"rem:brings-realisations","kind":"remark","title":"Realisations of Bring's surface","uses":["papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-brings-surface","papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/ex-c-quantum-universe"],"interprets":"papers/quantum-observable-universe/blocks/def-brings-surface","text":"brings-realisations.md","provenance":"authored","html":"<p><a id=\"rem:brings-realisations\"></a>\n<strong>Remark.</strong> <em>Realisations of Bring's surface</em></p>\n<p>Over an archimedean field <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">K</code> (e.g. <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{Q}</code>, <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{R}</code>, or <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{C}</code>), Bring's surface is a compact Riemann surface of genus <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">4</code>. The unit circle bundle <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">M_S</code> in <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">T^*\\Sigma_4</code> is a CR manifold of hypersurface type (real dimension <code class=\"language-math math-inline\">3</code>). It provides the archimedean realisation of the quantum observable universe (<a href=\"#ex:c-quantum-universe\"><code class=\"language-math math-inline\">\\mathbb{C}</code>-quantum universe</a>).</p>\n"}
